  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset landscape is undergoing a critical pivot marked by legislative friction, institutional maturation, and evolving cross-chain smart contract paradigms. The U.S. Digital Asset Market Clarity Act faces potential gridlock in the Senate as unresolved executive ethics provisions jeopardize the 60-vote threshold needed before the August recess. Institutionally, Bitcoin ETF inflows have moderated following 1H 2026 net outflows, transitioning the market from early spot ETF euphoria into structural balance sheet management where institutions hold over 31% of circulating supply. Concurrently, technical competition between Ethereum EVM dominance and Bitcoin native smart contracting via Clarity is intensifying. Non-custodial cross-chain liquidity tools and Clarity smart contracts are turning Bitcoin into active DeFi collateral, bridging BTC reserves directly into multi-chain financial applications without centralized bridge risks.",
